@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - REPORTING: ENGINE RUN SETTINGS</b>
  Home > Reporting > Engine run settings
  --
  <b>THE LIST</b>
  How the engine runs a report. A report binds one, and several reports can share it.
  [ Refresh ] | [ + Add ] | [ Workflows v ]
  "Search the name and description" | ^Used by reports: any^
  {#
    Name | Party | Groups | Threads | Reports | Last changed
    HK standard EOD (1 proposal) | ACME HK | 2 of 3 | 1 | 20 | 3 days ago
    HK four-thread simulation | ACME HK | 3 of 3 | 4 | 2 | 9 days ago
    US swaptions trial | ACME US | 2 of 3 | 2 | 0 | 12 days ago
  }
  1-3 of 3 | [ First ] | [ Previous ] | [ Next ] | [ Last ] | Page size ^15^
  --
  <b>ONE CONFIGURATION: HK STANDARD EOD</b>
  Version 6 - 2 of 3 groups set - bound by 20 reports - Editable
  [ Propose a change ]
  This configuration decides how the engine prepares its inputs and runs the job.
  It does not decide which model or engine prices a product. That is the pricing engine configuration.
  --
  <b>RELATED CONFIGURATIONS</b>
  Each row opens the configuration this report binds.
  {#
    Configuration | This report binds | What it decides
    Pricing engine configuration | EOD pricing | which model and engine price each product
    Today's market | ACME HK market | how the curves and surfaces are built
    Curve configuration | HK curves | how each curve is defined and bootstrapped
    Conventions | HK conventions | the market terms a trade is read on
  }
  --
  [ Details ] | [ Fixings and cash flows ] | [ Market and trade building ] | [ Execution ] | [ Used by ] | [ History ]
  --
  <b>FIXINGS AND CASH FLOWS</b>
  Changes the numbers - version 4
  A proposed version 5 waits for sign-off. Version 4 stays in force.
  "Search the settings" | [x] Set in this configuration | [ ] Changes the numbers | ^ Simple ^ | *Advanced*
  {#
    Setting | Value | Default
    Imply today's fixings | No | No
    Include today's cash flows | No | No
    Include reference date events | No | No
    Enrich index fixings | *Yes* | No
    Ignore fixing lag | 3 | 0
    Ignore fixing lead | 0 | 0
  }
  [ Show the documentation for every setting ]
  Enrich index fixings: fills a gap in an index's fixings with the previous fixing, or the next.
  Advanced: ORE argument /ORE/Setup/Parameter[@name='enrichIndexFixings']
             introduced in 1.8.0.7 - format: flag, Y or N - changes the numbers
  --
  <b>THE FOOT OF THE CARD</b>
  2 settings changed. The change reaches 20 reports.
  This section changes the numbers a run computes, so Save submits a proposal.
  [ Change reason ^Select a reason^ ] [ Commentary ]
  [ Cancel ] | [ Save as a proposal ]
  --
  The execution section is operational and saves directly, with a reason and a history entry.
}

@enduml
